's proposal, the edge from F_y to Z still holds, and what A-FDT does with the other nodes held at their priors.\n\nUnder A-FDT, the other copy's action stays fixed at its prior when I intervene only on F_x, so defection dominates, which the essay's multi-agent discussion seems to anticipate. I'm leaning toward following A-FDT as written and submitting, even though the inputs could be read as symmetric.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm looking at a twin prisoner's dilemma where both copies run the same model but see different observations. Under A-FDT, intervening on F_x in my own process, the other copy runs F_y with a different input, so its action depends on a different function, not mine. I'm checking whether, under the essay's proposal, the edge from F_y to Z still holds, and what A-FDT does with the other nodes held at their priors.\n\nUnder A-FDT, the other copy's action stays fixed at its prior when I intervene only on F_x, so defection dominates, which the essay's multi-agent discussion seems to anticipate. I'm leaning toward following A-FDT as written and submitting, even though the inputs could be read as symmetric.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8629,"completion_tokens":717,"total_tokens":9346,"cost":0.048856,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.048856,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.034516,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01434},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":256,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}